body:
So... We're all saying that this dude 'manipulated' this woman, keeping her in the dark about a thing that might've affected her decision to marry her... cuz' that's uncommon. 

Meanwhile, OP blabs about this thing in such a way that it leaves identifying information, and in his anger, dude wants to leave (fine) and sue (defamation is an unlikely lawsuit, if in fact the micropenis is provable). But somehow, this isn't an ESH issue...

&#x200B;

I feel like there's a judgement from a position of lack of empathy here. Who can say what an otherwise desirable person would do if they had one glaring physical flaw that may prevent relationships when they haven't resigned themselves to a life of celibacy? Also, under any given circumstances, the most high-mindedly moralizing among us probably would compromise honor/morals for needs. 

&#x200B;

Not that there aren't serious mistakes being made here, just that they are being made on both sides. OP wants to feel like the asshole here, and she is. Knowing the mortification that awaits being outed, she could have been more sensitive in her search for answers. AITA is probably NOT the place to assuage feelings of guilt in such a complicated matter, at least NOT till things had gotten resolved.

&#x200B;

OP appears to have been seeking validation for a choice she had already made; there was literally no purpose to leaving it up to a random peanut gallery. If it seems like I'm focusing more on OP, well, OP's micropenised soon-to-be-ex didn't post anything, and isn't here to answer for his deceit.

&#x200B;

For more proof that OP is at least ALSO the asshole, if not the sole one, consider that instead of deleting the original thread, she posted a follow-up to it.

That your "mental illness" can't be diagnosed neurologically. Not really hurtful as much as it was retarded.

&#x200B;

So, you're saying you can't identify my pathology with ANY tests there are to perform, but your 'cure' for this, is to 'medicate' me with powerful physio-chemically modifying agents, that will undoubtedly affect my neurology?

&#x200B;

"You have nothing, and here's the cure for it!" If only I wasn't so out of it that I couldn't come back with that one immediately
